07:04:58.851 --> 07:05:00.156
Yeah, over here?

07:05:00.156 --> 07:05:03.704
[INTERPOSING VOICES]

07:05:03.704 --> 07:05:04.371
DAVID J. MALAN: Nice.

07:05:04.371 --> 07:05:06.079
So at the end of the
for loop because you

07:05:06.079 --> 07:05:07.911
want to give the
program or our volunteer

07:05:07.911 --> 07:05:11.341
earlier a chance to go through all
of the doors, all of the numbers.

07:05:11.341 --> 07:05:14.061
But if you go through the whole
thing, through the whole loop,

07:05:14.061 --> 07:05:17.991
at the very end, you probably just
want to conclude not found backslash n

07:05:17.991 --> 07:05:20.421
and then return
something like positive 1

07:05:20.421 --> 07:05:22.401
just to signify that an error happened.

07:05:22.401 --> 07:05:24.531
And again, this was a
minor detail last week.

07:05:24.531 --> 07:05:28.731
Any time main is successful, the
programming convention is to return 0.

07:05:28.731 --> 07:05:30.211
That means all as well.

07:05:30.211 --> 07:05:33.381
And if something goes wrong, like you
didn't find what you're looking for,

07:05:33.381 --> 07:05:37.311
you might return something other than
0, like positive 1, maybe positive 2,

07:05:37.311 --> 07:05:39.563
or even negative numbers if you want.

07:05:39.563 --> 07:05:41.521
All right, well, let me
go ahead and save this.

07:05:41.521 --> 07:05:43.161
Let me do make numbers.

07:05:43.161 --> 07:05:45.591
Hopefully no syntax errors.

07:05:45.591 --> 07:05:46.881
All good so far.

07:05:46.881 --> 07:05:49.401
dot slash numbers, enter.

07:05:49.401 --> 07:05:51.861
All right, and it's found,
as I would hope it would be.

07:05:51.861 --> 07:05:55.071
And just as a little check, let's
