07:36:15.171 --> 07:36:17.571
You would look to the number to
the right or to the left of it,

07:36:17.571 --> 07:36:18.891
depending on which end you start at.

07:36:18.891 --> 07:36:21.474
And if it's out of order, you
would just start to swap things.

07:36:21.474 --> 07:36:22.711
And that seems reasonable.

07:36:22.711 --> 07:36:24.796
There's a whole bunch
of mistakes to fix here

07:36:24.796 --> 07:36:26.421
because things are pretty out of order.

07:36:26.421 --> 07:36:29.421
But probably, if you start to
solve small problems at a time,

07:36:29.421 --> 07:36:32.271
you can achieve the end result of
getting the whole thing sorted.

07:36:32.271 --> 07:36:35.181
Other instincts, if you were
just handed these numbers, how

07:36:35.181 --> 07:36:38.438
you might go about sorting them?

07:36:38.438 --> 07:36:39.021
How might you?

07:36:39.021 --> 07:36:40.217
Yeah, in the back.

07:36:40.217 --> 07:36:44.501
AUDIENCE: [INAUDIBLE]

07:36:44.501 --> 07:36:46.281
DAVID J. MALAN: OK, I like that.

07:36:46.281 --> 07:36:50.201
So to recap there, find the smallest
one first and put it at the beginning,

07:36:50.201 --> 07:36:51.431
if I heard you correctly.

07:36:51.431 --> 07:36:54.703
And then presumably, you could do
that again and again and again.

07:36:54.703 --> 07:36:57.411
And that would seem to give you
a couple of different algorithms.

07:36:57.411 --> 07:37:00.071
And if you all are attired here--

07:37:00.071 --> 07:37:03.161
