13:54:13.625 --> 13:54:15.292
than you might have in problem set five.

13:54:15.292 --> 13:54:18.529
But what's the trade-off going to be,
and what kinds of design decisions

13:54:18.529 --> 13:54:20.362
do we all now need to
be making consciously?

13:54:20.362 --> 13:54:22.822
Here we go, on the right, in Python.

13:54:22.822 --> 13:54:26.542
One Mississippi, two Mississippi,
three Mississippi, four Mississippi,

13:54:26.542 --> 13:54:30.592
five Mississippi, six Mississippi,
seven Mississippi, eight Mississippi,

13:54:30.592 --> 13:54:33.622
nine Mississippi, 10
Mississippi, 11 Mississippi,

13:54:33.622 --> 13:54:36.512
all right, so 10 or 11 seconds.

13:54:36.512 --> 13:54:38.502
So which one is better?

13:54:38.502 --> 13:54:43.072
Let's go to the group here, which
of these programs is the better one?

13:54:43.072 --> 13:54:47.302
How might you answer that question,
based on demonstration alone?

13:54:47.302 --> 13:54:48.052
What do you think?

13:54:48.052 --> 13:54:50.260
AUDIENCE: I think Python's
better for the programmer,

13:54:50.260 --> 13:54:54.369
more comfortable for the programmer,
but C is better for the user.

13:54:54.369 --> 13:54:56.202
DAVID J. MALAN: OK, so
