object-oriented programming.

14:27:51.022 --> 14:27:53.564
And we're going to keep seeing
examples of this dot operator.

14:27:53.564 --> 14:27:58.072
They are also immutable, so
to speak, I-M-M-U-T-A-B-L-E.

14:27:58.072 --> 14:28:01.702
Immutable means they cannot be
changed, which means, unlike C,

14:28:01.702 --> 14:28:05.272
you can't go into a string and
change its individual characters.

14:28:05.272 --> 14:28:08.002
You can make a copy of the
string that makes a change,

14:28:08.002 --> 14:28:10.220
but you can't change the
original string itself.

14:28:10.220 --> 14:28:12.262
This is both a little
annoying, maybe, sometimes.

14:28:12.262 --> 14:28:14.887
But it's also pretty protective,
because you can't do screw-ups

14:28:14.887 --> 14:28:18.202
like I did weeks ago, when I was
trying to copy S and call it T.

14:28:18.202 --> 14:28:19.792
