14:39:21.137 --> 14:39:22.722
You need that inverted logic.

14:39:22.722 --> 14:39:26.532
Unfortunately in Python,
there is no do while loop.

14:39:26.532 --> 14:39:27.822
There is a for loop.

14:39:27.822 --> 14:39:29.262
There is a while loop.

14:39:29.262 --> 14:39:32.112
And frankly, those are
enough to recreate this idea.

14:39:32.112 --> 14:39:35.682
And the way to do this in
Python, the Pythonic way, which

14:39:35.682 --> 14:39:38.682
is another term of art in the
community, is to say this.

14:39:38.682 --> 14:39:42.822
Deliberately induce an infinite loop,
while True, with capital T for true.

14:39:42.822 --> 14:39:46.452
And then do what you got to do,
like get an Int from a user,

14:39:46.452 --> 14:39:48.582
asking them for the
height of this thing.

14:39:48.582 --> 14:39:54.792
And then, if that is what you want, like
a number greater than zero, go ahead

14:39:54.792 --> 14:39:56.542
and break out of the loop.

14:39:56.542 --> 14:40:01.962
So this is how, in Python, you could
recreate the idea of a do while loop.

14:40:01.962 --> 14:40:03.837
You deliberately induce
an infinite loop.

14:40:03.837 --> 14:40:05.712
So something's going to
happen at least once.

14:40:05.712 --> 14:40:08.802
Then, if you get the answer
you want, you break out of it,

14:40:08.802 --> 14:40:10.852
effectively achieving the same logic.

14:40:10.852 --> 14:40:13.602
So this is the Pythonic way
of doing a do while loop.

