14:59:26.272 --> 14:59:29.392
But you and I are not dealing with
all the pointers underneath the hood.

14:59:29.392 --> 14:59:31.292
Python's doing that for us.

14:59:31.292 --> 14:59:34.957
So now, let's go ahead and get a
whole bunch of scores from the user.

14:59:34.957 --> 14:59:36.332
How about three of them in total.

14:59:36.332 --> 14:59:41.872
So for i in range of 3, let's go
ahead and grab a score from the user,

14:59:41.872 --> 14:59:44.332
using getInt, asking them for score.

14:59:44.332 --> 14:59:51.362
And then let's go ahead and append, to
the scores list, that particular score.

14:59:51.362 --> 14:59:53.722
So it turns out that a list,
and I could read the Python

14:59:53.722 --> 14:59:57.802
documentation to confirm as much,
lists have a function built into them,

14:59:57.802 --> 15:00:01.677
and functions built into objects
are generally known as methods,

15:00:01.677 --> 15:00:03.052
if you've heard that term before.

15:00:03.052 --> 15:00:05.842
Same idea, but whereas a function
kind of stands on its own,

15:00:05.842 --> 15:00:09.952
a method is a function built
into an object, like a list here.

15:00:09.952 --> 15:00:12.439
That's going to achieve the
same result. Strictly speaking,

15:00:12.439 --> 15:00:13.522
I don't need the variable.

15:00:13.522 --> 15:00:17.125
Just like in C, I could tighten this
up and do something like this as well.

15:00:17.125 --> 15:00:19.042
But, I don't know, I
