15:06:02.572 --> 15:06:07.032
So if you want access to the
argument vector, argv, you import it.

15:06:07.032 --> 15:06:11.622
And it turns out, there's another
module in Python, or library in Python

15:06:11.622 --> 15:06:15.702
called CIS, and you can import from
the system this thing called argv.

15:06:15.702 --> 15:06:17.879
So same idea, different place.

15:06:17.879 --> 15:06:19.462
Now I'm going to go ahead and do this.

15:06:19.462 --> 15:06:24.342
Let's write a program that just requires
