15:45:12.352 --> 15:45:15.532
Now that you've played with them
or used them in past real world,

15:45:15.532 --> 15:45:20.602
what's the utility of a CSV file versus
something like Excel, for instance?

15:45:20.602 --> 15:45:24.352
Why CSV in the first place?

15:45:24.352 --> 15:45:25.372
Any instincts?

15:45:25.372 --> 15:45:26.200
Yeah?

15:45:26.200 --> 15:45:28.072
AUDIENCE: Because it's just a text file?

15:45:28.072 --> 15:45:29.947
DAVID J. MALAN: OK, so
storage is compelling.

15:45:29.947 --> 15:45:33.052
A simple text file with ASCII or
Unicode text is probably pretty small.

15:45:33.052 --> 15:45:33.632
I like that.

15:45:33.632 --> 15:45:35.443
Other thoughts?

15:45:35.443 --> 15:45:36.526
AUDIENCE: Structure of it?

15:45:36.526 --> 15:45:37.860
DAVID J. MALAN: Yeah, well said.

15:45:37.860 --> 15:45:40.102
It's just a simple text
format, but using conventions

15:45:40.102 --> 15:45:43.672
like commas you can represent the
idea of columns using new lines,

15:45:43.672 --> 15:45:45.772
backslash ends invisibly
at the end of your lines,

15:45:45.772 --> 15:45:47.342
you can create the idea of rows.

15:45:47.342 --> 15:45:49.342
So it's a very simple
way of implementing what

15:45:49.342 --> 15:45:51.952
we might call a flat-file database.

15:45:51.952 --> 15:45:54.202
It's a way of storing
data in a flat, that is,

15:45:54.202 --> 15:45:57.652
very simple file that's just
pure ASCII or Unicode text.

15:45:57.652 --> 15:46:00.682
And more compellingly, I dare
say, is that with a CSV file,

15:46:00.682 --> 15:46:02.204
it's completely portable.

15:46:02.204 --> 15:46:04.162
Something is portable in
the world of computing

15:46:04.162 --> 15:46:07.252
if it means you can use it on a Mac
or a PC running this operating system,

15:46:07.252 --> 15:46:08.092
or this other one.

15:46:08.092 --> 15:46:10.822
And portability is nice because if
I were to download an Excel file,

15:46:10.822 --> 15:46:13.102
there'd be a whole bunch of
people in this room and online

15:46:13.102 --> 15:46:15.532
who couldn't download it because
they haven't bought Microsoft Excel

15:46:15.532 --> 15:46:16.282
or installed it.

15:46:16.282 --> 15:46:21.022
Or if they have a Mac, or if it's
a .numbers file in the Mac world,

15:46:21.022 --> 15:46:22.952
a PC user might not be
able to download it.

15:46:22.952 --> 15:46:25.142
So a CSV is indeed very portable.

