and increase the counter.

16:22:58.072 --> 16:23:00.382
So it turns out that the
regular expression library

16:23:00.382 --> 16:23:04.432
has a function called search that
takes as its first argument a pattern,

16:23:04.432 --> 16:23:07.312
and then, as its second
argument the string you

16:23:07.312 --> 16:23:09.502
want to analyze for that pattern.

16:23:09.502 --> 16:23:13.222
So it's sort of looking for a needle
in this haystack, from left to right.

