17:09:41.952 --> 17:09:44.622
If you go to most any website
on the internet today,

17:09:44.622 --> 17:09:48.762
and you, for instance, log in, odds are
you're typing a username and password,

17:09:48.762 --> 17:09:49.602
clicking Submit.

17:09:49.602 --> 17:09:50.772
What's then happening?

17:09:50.772 --> 17:09:53.352
Well, the website might not
be implemented in Python

17:09:53.352 --> 17:09:56.952
but it's probably implemented in some
language, Python, JavaScript, Java,

17:09:56.952 --> 17:09:58.452
Ruby, something else.

17:09:58.452 --> 17:10:03.672
And that language is probably using
something like a relational database

17:10:03.672 --> 17:10:07.272
to use SQL to get your
username, get your password,

17:10:07.272 --> 17:10:09.339
and compare the two against
what you've typed in.

17:10:09.339 --> 17:10:11.922
And actually, it's hopefully not
getting your actual password,

17:10:11.922 --> 17:10:13.505
but something called the hash thereof.

17:10:13.505 --> 17:10:15.702
But there's probably a
database involved doing that.

17:10:15.702 --> 17:10:18.942
When you buy something on
