So let me go ahead
and open favorites.py.

17:11:05.082 --> 17:11:10.542
And let me go ahead and throw away
some of what we did earlier and really

17:11:10.542 --> 17:11:13.032
just now add a SQL to the mix.

17:11:13.032 --> 17:11:16.782
From the CS50 library, let's
import the SQL function.

17:11:16.782 --> 17:11:19.602
This will be useful to use
because most third-party libraries

17:11:19.602 --> 17:11:22.732
that deal with SQL and Python are
more complicated than they need to be.

17:11:22.732 --> 17:11:25.732
So I think you'll find
this library easier to use.

17:11:25.732 --> 17:11:27.122
Let's then do the following.

17:11:27.122 --> 17:11:29.242
Create a variable
called db for database.

17:11:29.242 --> 17:11:30.742
But I could call it anything I want.

17:11:30.742 --> 17:11:34.432
Let's use that you URI, which is
a fancy way of saying something

17:11:34.432 --> 17:11:43.132
that looks like a URL, but that actually
opens up a database on disk, that is,

17:11:43.132 --> 17:11:44.452
in the current folder.

17:11:44.452 --> 17:11:47.962
Let's now ask the user for a title by
