17:12:19.492 --> 17:12:28.042
I'm going to select the count
of shows from the favorites

17:12:28.042 --> 17:12:35.302
table, where the title the user
typed in is like this question mark.

17:12:35.302 --> 17:12:37.252
And why I'm doing that is as follows.

17:12:37.252 --> 17:12:40.942
Just like in C, when we had
percent S, in SQL for now,

17:12:40.942 --> 17:12:42.832
the analogue is going
to be a question mark.

17:12:42.832 --> 17:12:44.332
So same idea, different syntax.

17:12:44.332 --> 17:12:46.522
Instead of percent S,
it's just a question mark.

17:12:46.522 --> 17:12:51.622
And using a comma outside of this
first string, using CS50's execute

17:12:51.622 --> 17:12:54.682
function I can pass in
a SQL string, a command,

17:12:54.682 --> 17:12:59.177
then any arguments I want to plug
