20:39:39.682 --> 20:39:45.682
And now lastly, in my index.html,
the syntax as of today in Flask,

20:39:45.682 --> 20:39:49.792
is to do two curly braces and
then put the name of the variable

20:39:49.792 --> 20:39:51.354
that you want to plug in.

20:39:51.354 --> 20:39:53.622
So here's what we mean by a template.

20:39:53.622 --> 20:39:56.712
A template is like a blueprint
in the real world, where

20:39:56.712 --> 20:39:58.842
it's plans to make something.

20:39:58.842 --> 20:40:02.712
This is the plan to make a web page
that has all of this code literally,

20:40:02.712 --> 20:40:06.222
but there's this placeholder with
two curly braces here and here

20:40:06.222 --> 20:40:10.642
that says go ahead and plug in the
value of the name variable right there.

20:40:10.642 --> 20:40:13.212
So in this sense, it's similar
in spirit to our f strings

20:40:13.212 --> 20:40:14.742
