20:41:44.557 --> 20:41:50.142
AUDIENCE: Why do you say the
question mark in the URL?

20:41:50.142 --> 20:41:52.572
DAVID: Why do you need a
question mark in the URL?

20:41:52.572 --> 20:41:59.152
The short answer is just because that
is where key value pairs must go.

20:41:59.152 --> 20:42:02.752
If you're making a GET request
from a browser to a server,

20:42:02.752 --> 20:42:07.452
the convention, standardized by the
HTTP protocol, is to put them in the URL

20:42:07.452 --> 20:42:11.152
after the so-called route or
path, then a question mark.

20:42:11.152 --> 20:42:13.602
And it delineates what's
part of the root or the path,

20:42:13.602 --> 20:42:17.752
and what's part of the
human input to the right.

20:42:17.752 --> 20:42:18.562
Other questions?

