stupid, but it has two different roles.

20:43:08.362 --> 20:43:10.112
The thing to the left
of the equal sign is

20:43:10.112 --> 20:43:14.222
the name of the variable you plan to use
in the template, the thing on the right

20:43:14.222 --> 20:43:16.232
is the actual value you're assigning it.

20:43:16.232 --> 20:43:18.092
And this is because its general purpose.

