21:25:20.722 --> 21:25:24.770
Register-- oh, I'm
confusing our two examples.

21:25:24.770 --> 21:25:26.062
All right, I spotted the error.

21:25:26.062 --> 21:25:26.895
What did I do wrong?

21:25:29.362 --> 21:25:32.242
Unintentional.

21:25:32.242 --> 21:25:35.812
There's where I am, what did
I actually invent over here?

21:25:39.672 --> 21:25:42.902
Where did I screw up?

21:25:42.902 --> 21:25:44.562
Anyone?

21:25:44.562 --> 21:25:45.812
AUDIENCE: Register, not greet.

21:25:45.812 --> 21:25:46.520
DAVID: Thank you.

21:25:46.520 --> 21:25:47.612
So register, not greet.

21:25:47.612 --> 21:25:50.732
I had last example on my mind,
so the route should be register.

21:25:50.732 --> 21:25:54.122
Ironically, the function could be greet,
because that actually doesn't matter.

21:25:54.122 --> 21:25:57.792
But to keep ourselves sane, let's
use the one and the same words there.

21:25:57.792 --> 21:26:00.219
Let me go ahead now and
start Flask as intended.

21:26:00.219 --> 21:26:02.552
Let me reload the form just
to make sure all is working.

21:26:02.552 --> 21:26:06.902
Now, let me not cooperate and be
a bad user, clicking register--

21:26:06.902 --> 21:26:07.982
oh my God.

21:26:07.982 --> 21:26:10.652
OK, other unintended mistake.

21:26:10.652 --> 21:26:12.882
But this one we've seen before.

21:26:12.882 --> 21:26:15.722
Notice that by default,
route only support GET.

21:26:15.722 --> 21:26:18.722
So if I want to
specifically support POST,

21:26:18.722 --> 21:26:25.472
I have to pass in, by a methods
parameter, a list of allowed route

21:26:25.472 --> 21:26:28.352
methods that could be
GET comma POST, but if I

21:26:28.352 --> 21:26:32.222
don't have no need for a GET in
this context, I can just do POST.

21:26:32.222 --> 21:26:34.742
All right, now let's
do this one last time.

21:26:34.742 --> 21:26:37.442
Reload the form to make sure
everything's OK, click Register,

21:26:37.442 --> 21:26:39.195
and you are not registered.

21:26:39.195 --> 21:26:40.112
So it's catching that.

21:26:40.112 --> 21:26:42.529
All right, let me go ahead and
at least give them my name.

21:26:42.529 --> 21:26:43.262
Register.

21:26:43.262 --> 21:26:44.312
You are not registered.

21:26:44.312 --> 21:26:49.662
Fine, I'm going to go ahead and be
David with ultimate frisbee register.

21:26:49.662 --> 21:26:52.022
Huh.

21:26:52.022 --> 21:26:53.402
OK.

21:26:53.402 --> 21:26:58.542
What should I-- what
did I mean to do here?

21:26:58.542 --> 21:27:00.572
All right, so let's figure this out.

21:27:00.572 --> 21:27:04.712
How to debug something like this,
which is my third and final unintended,

21:27:04.712 --> 21:27:07.082
unforced error?

21:27:07.082 --> 21:27:10.352
How can we go about
troubleshooting this?

21:27:10.352 --> 21:27:13.202
Turn this into the teachable moment.

21:27:13.202 --> 21:27:15.782
All right, well first,
some safety checks.

21:27:15.782 --> 21:27:17.372
What did I actually submit?

21:27:17.372 --> 21:27:20.522
Let me go ahead and view page
source, a good rule of thumb.

21:27:20.522 --> 21:27:23.082
Look at the HTML that you
actually sent to the user.

21:27:23.082 --> 21:27:27.252
So here, I have an
input with a name name.

21:27:27.252 --> 21:27:29.712
So that's what I
intended, that looks OK.

21:27:29.712 --> 21:27:32.552
Ah, I see it already, even
though you, if you've never

21:27:32.552 --> 21:27:35.792
used a select menu, you might
not know what, apparently,

21:27:35.792 --> 21:27:41.912
is missing from here that I
did have for my text input.

21:27:41.912 --> 21:27:45.467
Just intuitively, logically.

21:27:45.467 --> 21:27:47.342
What's going through my
head, embarrassingly,

21:27:47.342 --> 21:27:51.692
is, all right, if my form thinks
that it's missing a name or a sport,

21:27:51.692 --> 21:27:55.472
how did I create a situation in which
name is blank or sport is blank?

21:27:55.472 --> 21:27:57.482
Well, name, I don't think
it's going to be blank

21:27:57.482 --> 21:28:01.262
because I explicitly gave
this text field a name name

21:28:01.262 --> 21:28:02.972
and that did work last time.

21:28:02.972 --> 21:28:06.422
I've now given a second input
in the form of the select menu.

21:28:06.422 --> 21:28:13.112
But what seems to be missing here
that I'm assuming exists here?

21:28:13.112 --> 21:28:16.382
It's just a dumb mistake I made.

21:28:16.382 --> 21:28:19.448
What might be missing here?

21:28:19.448 --> 21:28:23.552
If request.form gives you all of
the inputs that the user might

21:28:23.552 --> 21:28:26.552
have typed in, let me
go into my actual code

21:28:26.552 --> 21:28:30.452
here in my form and name equals sport.

21:28:30.452 --> 21:28:32.472
I just didn't give a name to that input.

21:28:32.472 --> 21:28:34.652
So it exists, and the
browser doesn't care.

21:28:34.652 --> 21:28:36.485
It's still going to
display the form to you,

21:28:36.485 --> 21:28:40.212
it just hasn't given it a unique name
to actually transmit to the server.

21:28:40.212 --> 21:28:42.552
So now, if I'm not going
to put my foot in my mouth,

21:28:42.552 --> 21:28:44.742
I think that's what I did wrong.

21:28:44.742 --> 21:28:46.712
And again, my process
for figuring that out

21:28:46.712 --> 21:28:49.044
was looking at my code,
thinking through logically,

21:28:49.044 --> 21:28:50.252
is this right, is this right?

21:28:50.252 --> 21:28:52.422
No, I was missing the name there.

21:28:52.422 --> 21:28:55.382
So let's run Flask,
let's reload the form

21:28:55.382 --> 21:28:59.942
just to make sure it's all defaults
again, type in my name and type

21:28:59.942 --> 21:29:04.442
in ultimate frisbee, crossing
my fingers extra hard this time.

21:29:04.442 --> 21:29:05.232
And there.

21:29:05.232 --> 21:29:06.099
You are registered.

21:29:06.099 --> 21:29:06.932
So I can emphasize--

21:29:06.932 --> 21:29:08.665
I did not intend to
screw up in that way,

21:29:08.665 --> 21:29:10.832
but that's exactly the right
kind of thought process

21:29:10.832 --> 21:29:12.152
to diagnose issues like this.

21:29:12.152 --> 21:29:16.022
Go back to the basics, go back to what
HTTP and what HTML forms are all about,

21:29:16.022 --> 21:29:18.432
and just rule things in and out.

21:29:18.432 --> 21:29:21.182
There's only a finite number of
ways I could have screwed that up.

21:29:21.182 --> 21:29:22.054
Yeah?

21:29:22.054 --> 21:29:23.410
AUDIENCE: Are you [INAUDIBLE].

21:29:25.582 --> 21:29:27.082
DAVID: Excuse-- say a little louder?

21:29:27.082 --> 21:29:30.982
AUDIENCE: I don't understand why
name equals sport [INAUDIBLE]..

21:29:30.982 --> 21:29:33.632
DAVID: Why did name equal
sport address the problem?

21:29:33.632 --> 21:29:35.872
Well, let's first go back to the HTML.

21:29:35.872 --> 21:29:43.172
Previously, it was just the reality that
I had this user input dropdown menu,

21:29:43.172 --> 21:29:44.602
but I never gave it a name.

21:29:44.602 --> 21:29:47.932
But names, or more
generally, key value pairs,

21:29:47.932 --> 21:29:51.212
is how information is sent
from a form to the server.

21:29:51.212 --> 21:29:56.422
So if there's no name, there's no key to
send, even if the human types a value.

21:29:56.422 --> 21:30:00.082
It would be like nothing equals ultimate
frisbee, and that just doesn't work.

21:30:00.082 --> 21:30:02.432
The browser is just
not going to send it.

21:30:02.432 --> 21:30:08.332
However, in app.py, I was naively
assuming that in my requests form,

21:30:08.332 --> 21:30:11.062
there would be a name called
quote unquote "sport."

21:30:11.062 --> 21:30:13.702
It could have been anything,
but I was assuming it was sport.

21:30:13.702 --> 21:30:15.532
But I never told the form that.

21:30:15.532 --> 21:30:19.022
And if I really wanted to dig in,
we could do a little something more.

21:30:19.022 --> 21:30:22.012
Let me go back to the
way it was a moment ago.

21:30:22.012 --> 21:30:25.802
Let me get rid of the name
of the sport dropdown menu.

21:30:25.802 --> 21:30:30.982
Let me rerun Flask down here
and reload the form itself

21:30:30.982 --> 21:30:33.412
after it finishes being served.

21:30:33.412 --> 21:30:34.582
And now, let me do this.

21:30:34.582 --> 21:30:39.277
View Developer Tools, and then let me
watch the Network tab, which recall,

21:30:39.277 --> 21:30:41.152
we played around with
a little bit last week.

21:30:41.152 --> 21:30:44.334
And we also played around with Curl,
which let us see the HTTP requests.

21:30:44.334 --> 21:30:46.042
Here's another-- here's
what I would have

21:30:46.042 --> 21:30:49.412
done if I still wasn't seeing the error
and was really embarrassed on stage.

21:30:49.412 --> 21:30:53.512
I would have typed in my name as before,
I would have chosen ultimate frisbee.

21:30:53.512 --> 21:30:55.252
I would have clicked register.

21:30:55.252 --> 21:30:59.242
And now, I would have
looked at the HTTP request.

21:30:59.242 --> 21:31:01.342
And I would click on Register here.

21:31:01.342 --> 21:31:04.942
And just like we did last week, I
would go down to the request down here.

21:31:04.942 --> 21:31:07.672
And there's a whole lot of stuff
that we can typically ignore.

21:31:07.672 --> 21:31:10.792
But here, let me zoom
in, way at the bottom,

21:31:10.792 --> 21:31:13.132
what Chrome's developer
tools are doing for me,

21:31:13.132 --> 21:31:16.142
it's showing me all of the
form data that was submitted.

21:31:16.142 --> 21:31:18.712
So this really would have
been my telltale clue.

21:31:18.712 --> 21:31:21.982
I'm just not sending the sport,
even if the human typed it in.

21:31:21.982 --> 21:31:23.992
And logically, because
I've done this before,

21:31:23.992 --> 21:31:26.932
that must mean I didn't
give the thing a name.

21:31:26.932 --> 21:31:28.102
But another good tool.

21:31:28.102 --> 21:31:31.372
Like good programmers, web developers
are using these kinds of tools

21:31:31.372 --> 21:31:32.422
all the time.

21:31:32.422 --> 21:31:34.160
They're not writing bug-free code.

21:31:34.160 --> 21:31:35.452
That's not the point to get to.

21:31:35.452 --> 21:31:38.542
The point to get to is
being a good diagnostician,

21:31:38.542 --> 21:31:40.552
I would say, in these cases.

21:31:40.552 --> 21:31:45.552
OK, other questions on this?

21:31:45.552 --> 21:31:46.812
Yeah.

21:31:46.812 --> 21:31:52.152
AUDIENCE: What if you want to
edit one HTML in CSS, [INAUDIBLE]..

21:31:52.152 --> 21:31:54.444
DAVID: I'm sorry, a little bit louder?

21:31:54.444 --> 21:31:57.012
AUDIENCE: If you want to
edit in CSS or anything,

21:31:57.012 --> 21:32:01.422
in HTML, once you have to fix
the template, how do you that?

21:32:01.422 --> 21:32:05.532
DAVID: So how would you edit
CSS if you have these templates?

21:32:05.532 --> 21:32:07.842
That process we'll
actually see before long.

21:32:07.842 --> 21:32:09.467
It's almost going to be the exact same.

21:32:09.467 --> 21:32:12.550
Just to give you a teaser for this,
and you'll do this in the problem set,

21:32:12.550 --> 21:32:15.402
but we'll give you some distribution
code to automate this process.

21:32:15.402 --> 21:32:17.862
You can absolutely still
do something like this.

21:32:17.862 --> 21:32:22.661
Link href equals quote
unquote "styles" dot

21:32:22.661 --> 21:32:27.371
CSS rel equals style sheet, that's one
of the techniques we showed last week.

21:32:27.371 --> 21:32:31.422
The only difference today, using Flask,
is that all of your static files,

21:32:31.422 --> 21:32:34.041
by convention, should go
in your static folder.

21:32:34.041 --> 21:32:36.072
So the change you would
make in your layout

21:32:36.072 --> 21:32:40.002
would be to say that styles dot
CSS is in your static folder.

21:32:40.002 --> 21:32:43.991
And then, if I go into
my FroshIMS directory,

21:32:43.991 --> 21:32:46.331
I can create a static folder.

21:32:46.331 --> 21:32:48.822
I can CD into it,
nothing's there by default.

21:32:48.822 --> 21:32:51.762
But if I now code a
file called styles.css,

21:32:51.762 --> 21:32:54.822
I could now do something like this body.

21:32:54.822 --> 21:33:05.982
And in here, I could say background
color, say FF0000 to make it red.

21:33:05.982 --> 21:33:10.212
Let me go ahead now and restart
Flask in the FroshIMS directory.

21:33:10.212 --> 21:33:12.822
Cross my fingers because
I'm doing this on the fly.

21:33:12.822 --> 21:33:16.161
Go back to my form and reload.

21:33:16.161 --> 21:33:19.752
Voila, now we've tied together
last week's stuff as well.

21:33:19.752 --> 21:33:22.854
If I answered the right question?

21:33:22.854 --> 21:33:27.202
AUDIENCE: [INAUDIBLE] change
one page and not the other.

21:33:27.202 --> 21:33:30.202
DAVID: If you want to change one page
and not the other in terms of CSS?

21:33:30.202 --> 21:33:31.012
AUDIENCE: Yes.

21:33:31.012 --> 21:33:32.122
DAVID: That depends.

21:33:32.122 --> 21:33:36.952
In that case, you might want to have
different CSS files for each page

21:33:36.952 --> 21:33:38.152
if they're different.

21:33:38.152 --> 21:33:42.382
You could use different classes in one
template than you did in the other.

21:33:42.382 --> 21:33:43.802
There's different ways to do that.

21:33:43.802 --> 21:33:47.752
You could even have a
placeholder in your layout

21:33:47.752 --> 21:33:52.222
that allows you to plug in
the URL of a specific style

21:33:52.222 --> 21:33:53.662
sheet in your individual files.

21:33:53.662 --> 21:33:56.432
But that starts to get
more complicated quickly.

21:33:56.432 --> 21:33:58.172
So in short, you can absolutely do it.

21:33:58.172 --> 21:34:01.942
But typically, I would
say most websites try not

21:34:01.942 --> 21:34:03.652
to use different style Sheets per page.

21:34:03.652 --> 21:34:06.322
They reuse the styles
as much as they can.

21:34:06.322 --> 21:34:08.572
All right, let me go ahead
and revert this real quick.

21:34:08.572 --> 21:34:11.512
And let's start to add a little
bit more functionality here.

21:34:11.512 --> 21:34:14.392
I'm going to go ahead and just
remove the static folder just so as

21:34:14.392 --> 21:34:16.162
to not complicate things just yet.

21:34:16.162 --> 21:34:19.252
And let's go ahead and just play
around with a different user interface

21:34:19.252 --> 21:34:19.852
mechanism.

21:34:19.852 --> 21:34:23.265
In my form here, the dropdown
menu is perfectly fine.

21:34:23.265 --> 21:34:24.182
Nothing wrong with it.

21:34:24.182 --> 21:34:27.412
But suppose that I wanted to
change it to checkboxes instead.

21:34:27.412 --> 21:34:31.432
Maybe I want students to be able to
register for multiple sports instead.

21:34:31.432 --> 21:34:34.822
Well, it might make sense to
clean this up in a couple of ways.

21:34:34.822 --> 21:34:35.572
And let's do this.

21:34:35.572 --> 21:34:40.762
Before we even get into the checkboxes,
there's one subtle bad design here.

21:34:40.762 --> 21:34:45.212
Notice that I've hardcoded basketball,
soccer, and ultimate frisbee here.

21:34:45.212 --> 21:34:49.592
And if you recall, in app.py, I also
enumerated all three of those here.

21:34:49.592 --> 21:34:52.932
And any time you see copy paste
or the equivalent thereof,

21:34:52.932 --> 21:34:54.602
feels like we could do better.

21:34:54.602 --> 21:34:56.402
So what if I instead do this.

21:34:56.402 --> 21:35:00.712
What if I instead give myself
a global variable of Sports,

21:35:00.712 --> 21:35:03.112
I'll capitalize the word
just to connote that it's

21:35:03.112 --> 21:35:07.162
meant to be constant even though
Python does not have constants, per se.

21:35:07.162 --> 21:35:09.742
The first sport will be basketball.

21:35:09.742 --> 21:35:11.722
The second will be soccer.

21:35:11.722 --> 21:35:15.922
The third will be ultimate frisbee.

21:35:15.922 --> 21:35:19.942
Now I have one convenient
place to store all of my sports

21:35:19.942 --> 21:35:22.462
if it changes next semester
or next year or whatnot.

21:35:22.462 --> 21:35:24.472
But notice what I could do to.

21:35:24.472 --> 21:35:26.102
I could now do something like this.

21:35:26.102 --> 21:35:30.112
Let me pass into my
index template a variable

21:35:30.112 --> 21:35:34.462
called sports that's equal to
that global variable sports.

21:35:34.462 --> 21:35:37.792
Let me go into my index now,
and this is really, now,

21:35:37.792 --> 21:35:41.782
going to hint at the power of
templating and Jinja, in this case here.

21:35:41.782 --> 21:35:45.452
Let me go ahead and get rid of all
three of these hard coded options

21:35:45.452 --> 21:35:50.332
and let me show you some slightly
different syntax for sport, in sports.

21:35:50.332 --> 21:35:52.852
Then end for.

21:35:52.852 --> 21:35:54.872
We've not seen this end for syntax.

21:35:54.872 --> 21:35:57.692
There's like end block syntax,
but it's as simple as that.

21:35:57.692 --> 21:36:00.952
So you have a start and an end to your
block without indentation mattering.

21:36:00.952 --> 21:36:02.392
Watch what I can do here.

21:36:02.392 --> 21:36:08.482
Option curly brace
sport close curly brace.

21:36:08.482 --> 21:36:09.832
Let me save that.

21:36:09.832 --> 21:36:12.982
Let me go back into my
terminal window, do Flask run.

21:36:12.982 --> 21:36:16.162
And if I didn't mess up
here, let me go back to this.

21:36:16.162 --> 21:36:18.802
The red's going to go away
because I deleted my CSS.

21:36:18.802 --> 21:36:21.832
And now I still have a sport
dropdown and all of those sports

21:36:21.832 --> 21:36:22.772
are still there.

21:36:22.772 --> 21:36:24.352
I can make one more improvement now.

21:36:24.352 --> 21:36:27.302
I don't need to mention these
same sports manually in app.py.

21:36:27.302 --> 21:36:31.672
I can now just say if the
user's inputed sport is not

21:36:31.672 --> 21:36:35.070
in my global variable, sports,
and ask the same question.

21:36:35.070 --> 21:36:36.862
And this is really
handy because if there's

21:36:36.862 --> 21:36:41.002
another sport, for instance, that
gets added, like say football,

21:36:41.002 --> 21:36:43.922
all I have to do is
change my global variable.

21:36:43.922 --> 21:36:47.542
And if I reload the form now
and look in the dropdown, boom,

21:36:47.542 --> 21:36:49.732
now I have support for a fourth sport.

21:36:49.732 --> 21:36:51.422
And I can keep adding and adding there.

21:36:51.422 --> 21:36:55.012
So here's where templating starts
to get really powerful in that

21:36:55.012 --> 21:37:00.472
now, in this template, I'm using
Jinja's for loop syntax, which

21:37:00.472 --> 21:37:02.962
is almost identical to
Python here, except you

21:37:02.962 --> 21:37:06.262
need the curly brace and the percent
sign and you need the weird ending

21:37:06.262 --> 21:37:07.132
and for.

21:37:07.132 --> 21:37:08.812
But it's the same idea as in Python.

21:37:08.812 --> 21:37:13.072
Iterating over something with a for loop
lets you generate more and more HTML.

21:37:13.072 --> 21:37:14.992
And this is like every
website out there.

21:37:14.992 --> 21:37:15.862
For instance, Gmail.

21:37:15.862 --> 21:37:19.852
When you visit your inbox and you
see all of this big table of emails,

21:37:19.852 --> 21:37:22.492
Google has not hardcoded
your emails manually.

21:37:22.492 --> 21:37:24.322
They have grabbed them from a database.

21:37:24.322 --> 21:37:26.072
They have some kind
of for loop like this,

21:37:26.072 --> 21:37:32.057
and are just outputting table row after
table row or div after div dynamically.

21:37:32.057 --> 21:37:34.432
All right, so now, let's go
ahead and change this, maybe,

21:37:34.432 --> 21:37:40.232
to, oh, how about little
checkboxes or radio buttons.

21:37:40.232 --> 21:37:41.572
So let me go ahead and do this.

21:37:41.572 --> 21:37:46.432
Instead of a select menu, I'm going to
go ahead and do something like this.

21:37:46.432 --> 21:37:52.352
For each of these sports let me go
ahead and output, not an option,

21:37:52.352 --> 21:37:55.282
but let me go ahead and
output an input tag,

21:37:55.282 --> 21:37:59.302
the name for which is quote
unquote "sport," the type of which

21:37:59.302 --> 21:38:05.002
is checkbox, the value of which is
going to be the current "sport,"

21:38:05.002 --> 21:38:09.404
